text = _release_expand(f"""# Eleven new information links to dental material and design nodes

Run **`./run_all.sh`** here. Command reads local originals, replays relevant earlier cells, checks values and creates references, results and figure. It writes in this lane directory and its small data directory under `@DENTAL_EXTERNAL_ROOT@/storage`; it does not install or rebuild the graph.

The consumer receives observations absent from a simplified representation: previous specimen loading, defect location, MEASURED pore shape or plastic material response. Eleven new links in `notes/expansion/information_links_proof_lane3_20261003.jsonl` are **information_link**, **OPEN**, **PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW**. Scoped available inputs and benchmarks, not validated improved dental predictions.

{table}

Original values with file/row/table cell locators in `FACIT.csv` and `FACIT.json`. Full raw bindings and source hashes in `LINK_CONTRACTS.json`, `SOURCE_MANIFEST.json` and `raw/`. Original point/specimen identities retained; consumer-derived correlations/group means separate as POPULATION. No source node promoted. Eleven links derive from **four data lineages** (Ley, Luo, EBSD, PLA), not eleven independent experiments.

![Local originals and what simplified representations miss](information_links_figure.png)

**What fails.** Older cells 138 specimens are {m['L01']['characterized_site_rows']} fracture site rows, {m['L01']['unique_test_regions']} test regions and {m['L01']['unique_specimens']} physical specimens under the composite key. Prior 10 million retest cycles belong to history; terminal cycles are not lifetime from an unloaded specimen. Rank adjustment is neither exact matching nor causal identification. L02 first-fracture-site sensitivity per specimen is {m['L02']['first_site_per_specimen_partial']:.3f}, compared with row-based {m['L02']['by_mode']['all']['partial_rank_correlation']:.3f}.

Low sphericity does not measure stress concentration Kt; largest observed pore is not identified fracture initiation. Grain diameter ratio reveals unresolved definitions, not a proven stereological transform. EBSD components use c-axis angle, not full crystal misorientation; diameter statistics **PHENOMENOLOGICAL**, requiring symmetry-correct segmentation and larger fields of view. Area-weighted texture tensor alone does not identify elastic anisotropy.

First lattice peak is algorithmically extracted, not independently confirmed buckling. Elastic projection uses observed peak strain and is a retrospective deviation check; no general nonidentifiability theorem. PLA coefficients cannot transfer to Ti64. Candidate **L11 rejected** because `Resumen` lacks explicit modulus units. Relative errors/historical calculations preserved in `REJECTED_L11.json`; absolute table MPa values not established. Older free exponent fit also reads test density and is not a clean held-out test.

Controls are declared benchmark simplifications; clinical practice was not mapped here. Missing retest history misassigns {r['controls']['L01']['misassigned_fracture_site_rows']} terminal cycle values; isotropic tensor and sphericity=1 differ from raw observations; mean shape misses extreme shape. Historical Hollomon/linear test is a replay task, not this round method competition. {valid['source_values_passed']} original value checks pass; {valid['fault_injections_rejected']} injected value/contract faults rejected. Hollomon replay fails its original 15 MPa gate. Successful extraction must not conceal an earlier negative research result.

**Attrition.** Of 22 explicitly reviewed link proposals, 11 retained; **11/22 = 50.00%** rejected: six already established, four stronger interpretations unsupported, one missing explicit original units. Excluding duplicates **5/16 = 31.25%**. Not attrition over all 196 index records; others lack primary source review here. ISO14801 RAW36, Park, CBCT, glass ceramic tail and earlier porosity/lattice exponent links not reestablished.

Data level: {a['fatigue']['excluded_no_characterization']}/{a['fatigue']['input_rows']} fatigue rows lack defect characterization. Two of 35 pore files excluded from new quantitative analyses: `sample 5.csv` and `sample 16.csv` lack diameter units and use `sorted` rather than sphericity. Older replays retain original 35 files with a different analysis set; do not mix with new 33-file results. Observations retained. Lattice: {a['lattice']['curve_sheets_loaded']} readable curves, {a['lattice']['curves_retained_first_peak']} pass frozen extraction; negative stress artifacts flagged separately. Exact denominators in `ATTRITION.json`.

| Local dataset | Origin and reference | License status for this delivery |
|---|---|---|
| Ti64 PBF fatigue | Ley, Ngo, Lewandowski, DOI 10.3390/data11040081, original supplement Table S1 CSV | UNKNOWN in reviewed local files; originals not redistributed |
| Ti64 PSP, pores, grains, curves | Luo et al., DOI 10.1016/j.addma.2022.102915; Zenodo 6587905, original workbook B2/H2 | UNKNOWN in reviewed local files; originals not redistributed |
| Ti64 EBSD | Original `Gaussian_1.ctf` and `Tailored_beam.ctf`, header and older wave791 cell | UNKNOWN; external deposition locator not recovered locally; originals not redistributed |
| PLA compression | Mendeley nvzrft8c7d; `Compressivedata.xlsx` | UNKNOWN in reviewed local files; originals not redistributed |

No patient data or clinical recommendation. Reproduction expectations frozen before execution in `FROZEN_PREDICTIONS.json`; not blind predictions of a new measurement. Demo cost: {r['cost']['wall_seconds']:.1f} s, peak RSS {r['cost']['max_rss_kib'] / 1024:.1f} MiB, one thread, {r['cost']['data_bytes'] / 1000000.0:.1f} MB intermediates. Prior reading/selection excluded from this execution time.
""")
